<title>POLAND: NBP drains PLN 90 mln from Polish money market.</title>
<headline>NBP drains PLN 90 mln from Polish money market.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland drained 60 million zlotys from the market for seven days and 30 million for 14 days after banks bid to place a total of 118 million at the reverse repo auction, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The bank drained the market for 14 days at an unchanged maximum rate of 22.15 percent and for seven days at 22.09 percent, down from the previous maximum rate of 22.10.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
